// Title: Fax Service DLL Search Order Hijack
// Sigma ID: 828af599-4c53-4ed2-ba4a-a9f835c434ea
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: NVISO
// Date: 2020-05-04 | Modified: 2022-06-02
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: The Fax service attempts to load ualapi.dll, which is non-existent. An attacker can then
//   (side)load their own malicious DLL using this service.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://windows-internals.com/faxing-your-way-to-system/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_ualapi.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\fxssvc.exe" and FolderPath endswith "ualapi.dll") and (not(FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\"))
